# Line endings, pinned - so the same file is byte-identical on both laptops.
#
# Without this, Git's Windows default (core.autocrlf=true) checks files out as CRLF.
# That matters here beyond taste: deck/asciify_notes.py writes TEAM_NOTES.md with
# newline="\n" explicitly, so a CRLF checkout means the first run rewrites all 540
# lines and `git diff` shows the whole file changed when nothing did. Normalising to
# LF everywhere makes the two machines agree.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-native launchers keep CRLF - cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only .bat files.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary: never touch, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.pptx binary
*.potx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary
*.tif binary
*.tiff binary
*.pt binary
*.pth binary
*.npy binary
*.npz binary

# Generated - collapse in PR diffs so review stays readable.
frontend/package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff
